WEBVTT

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:05.640
<i>Monsters threaten human life.</i>

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.670
<i>They are opposed by brave adventurers!</i>

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:14.480
<i>And I, Alvin, am one of them!</i>

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:18.490
Now in a party with Carla, the healer,

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:21.390
my journey continues!

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
My Healer!

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:57.840
<b>The owner of the inn they visit seems very nice, but...</b>

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:57.840
<b>Inn Stay! Burin</b>

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:57.830
Excuse me.

00:01:57.830 --> 00:01:59.460
We'd like a room for the night.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:00.430
Oink.

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:02.890
Welcome to Stay! Burin.

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:04.590
That's a wonderful name for an inn.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:07.220
Oink. Thank you very much.

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:08.900
How many in your party?

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.460
Just me and one wannabe goblin.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.560
I don't want to stay in a pigsty—

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:16.460
It's an inn.

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:17.840
But it really looks like—

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:19.320
It's all people here.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:20.970
But he keeps saying "oink."

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:21.910
Drop it.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:23.590
What was that she said?

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:25.710
Oh, ignore her.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:27.380
It's just goblin nonsense.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:32.370
Oh, would you like me to prepare 
your dinner for the night?

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:35.120
I do a bit of cooking on the side!

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:38.600
Or maybe it's a butcher's shop?

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.000
It's an <i>inn</i>.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:41.070
What's on the menu for tonight?

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:42.020
Tonkatsu!

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.190
That's... deep-fried pork?

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:47.180
Oink.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:52.290
Is tonkatsu tastier when you murder 
your own kind to make it?!

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:53.610
It's ton-conscionable!

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:54.610
Will you just...

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:56.950
You can't say that to his face!

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:58.730
Your rudeness is off the charts today!

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:02.990
But you were thinking the same thing I was!

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:05.970
It's pathetic to act like you 
have the moral high ground!

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.630
And I have never spoken 
anything but the truth!

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:10.250
I already know that's a bald-faced lie—

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:11.880
And what's with those moves?!

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:13.950
I got motion-sick.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:16.470
I wish you'd spit up your evil soul.

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:18.830
You really didn't notice?

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:20.050
I wonder if that ugly...

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:24.210
I mean, unique helmet of yours has 
a curse to reduce your perception.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.750
What are you talking about?

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:30.290
I'm saying, that pig is not human!

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.770
Everyone knows that pigs aren't human.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:34.560
But that's what I'm—

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.710
Oh, eternal darkness!

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:37.770
Hey.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:41.540
Are you calling me a pig?

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:43.000
See? He's mad!

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.500
You've got him enraged!

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:46.250
Did you say he's a Landrace?

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:48.540
Are you just hungry or something?

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.300
You mock me...

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:52.480
Wh-What's he doing?

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:54.490
He's shown his true self.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.000
Very well...

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.800
You'll see what kind of pig I am...

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.810
at the cost of your lives!

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:02.570
A monster!

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:03.950
Please, be careful!

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:06.690
Dark elves find his breed of 
monster particularly detestable!

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:08.980
Seems irrelevant, since you're a goblin!

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:10.340
Oink!

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:14.100
How dare you say that?!

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:17.070
He was disguised as a human?

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:18.030
Maybe he's a tanuki?

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:21.470
Bah! A pox on you all!

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:23.560
You'll pay for calling me a pig!

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:27.400
I am a proud member of the orc race! Oink!

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.690
His true face is incredible!

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:30.080
Hang on a minute!

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.600
I just realized something outrageous!

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:35.130
I must be an angel, to have 
noticed something like this!

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:36.890
Did you? That's great.

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:38.880
But I suspect your realization 
will further complicate things,

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.080
so could you keep it to yourself?

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.760
I assumed the innkeeper was a pig, but...

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.140
Yeah, just can't keep anything to herself.

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:47.490
But he said, "Baa" just now!

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:49.760
That suggests he's not a pig, but a sheep!

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:52.780
He had me fooled... 
I was so sure he was a pig!

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:54.930
Actually, I'm an orc!

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:56.170
Oink! Oink!

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:57.530
You heard the man.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.560
But he said "Baa" earlier!

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:01.860
I said "Bah," not "Baa"!

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.010
What? So you <i>are</i> a pig?

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:06.880
I'm not a pig! I'm an orc!

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:09.000
A pork? That's still a pig.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.630
Bah! I'm an orc! An orc!

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:14.400
He said, "Baa" again! He's a total sheep!

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.620
It's not that kind of "Bah"!

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.860
Oh, give me a break! Ugh!

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:20.290
"Ook"? You're a monkey now?

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:21.530
That's a bit of a stretch!

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:23.000
I'm not sure how you expect 
us to believe that!

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.110
Shut up!

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:27.410
You can't taunt an orc 
and get off scot-free!

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:29.310
How much for a room, then?

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:30.630
Oh, a room for two?

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:31.610
No, screw that!

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:33.100
You're gonna have to fight me! One-on-one!

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:34.590
Hang on a minute!

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:36.990
I know she picked this fight all on her own,

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:38.730
but a duel seems a bit much...

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:39.530
Very well.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:41.440
All right, you're on!

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:45.760
If you win, you can call me a pig, 
a sheep, or anything you want!

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:46.860
Very well.

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:51.050
And if I lose, I will also 
treat you like a pig.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.400
That seems only fair.

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:53.580
You're ruthless.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.180
That's ridiculous!

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:58.500
It means you're treating me like 
a pig whether I win or lose!

00:05:58.500 --> 00:05:59.910
Then, let us begin!

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:01.750
Hang on a minute! We 
aren't finished talking!

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.240
First comes...

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:04.140
And we're doing rock-paper-scissors?!

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:05.270
Pork!

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:11.880
That's a joke on "Rock" and "Pork," I think.

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:13.360
I mean, I got that...

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:17.280
I've just taken so much abuse today, 
it's hard to have the appropriate reaction.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:19.770
Hey, no need to spare her feelings.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:20.310
Just say she bombed—

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:22.950
What is it?

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:25.310
I s-suddenly feel feverish!

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:27.890
It's e-explosive damage.

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:29.360
"Bombed" means your joke didn't land.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:30.690
Should I ask you to kill me?

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:34.080
The fool completely imploded!

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:36.980
But she seems like the type that 
never learns until she suffers,

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:38.260
so I guess it serves her right!

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:39.720
I'm with you there.

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:43.380
But... technically, it <i>is </i>
my job to protect her!

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.110
I won't allow you to harm her!

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:47.220
Always wanted to say something like that!

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:51.960
Then I'll have to flatten you, as well!

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:52.810
Jump!

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:53.210
Jump—

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:55.160
Hecaton Press!

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:56.090
Such a short jump...

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:57.790
Oink!

00:06:58.820 --> 00:06:59.810
What's wrong?

00:07:00.110 --> 00:07:03.080
I think I broke my leg on the landing.

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:04.190
Lose some weight?

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:06.920
Can you cast a healing spell on him?

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:08.600
I seriously can't watch this...

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:12.340
I don't know any spells that 
work on flightless pigs.

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:14.190
I could put him out of his misery, though.

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:16.940
You sure about that? 
You could get on his good side.

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:18.950
Don't move!

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:21.080
I'll cast a healing spell on you now!

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:24.710
Though I doubt there's anything you 
can do to get on his good side now...

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:25.780
Oink...

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:27.920
Y-You would save me?

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:28.700
But why?

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:33.110
Does one need a reason to 
save another from suffering?

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:35.670
Just don't go charging him afterwards, okay?

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:40.170
At least try to deny it?

00:07:40.470 --> 00:07:42.660
Oink. O, Holy Woman!

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:44.350
I think he's got brain damage.

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:46.730
Oh, you flatterer. I hear that all the time!

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:48.100
And she's even worse!

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:50.320
But first, Mr. Innkeeper...

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:52.370
I do have a question for you.

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:56.920
It's about the travelers and adventurers 
who have stayed at your inn before us.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:58.360
Oh, that's right.

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:03.290
The only reason an orc would go out of his way 
to disguise himself as human and run an inn...

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:04.300
Can it be...?!

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:05.740
Oink.

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:07.460
I guess the pig is up.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:09.320
You work for a slaughterhouse?

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:13.100
I'm in the presence of a holy woman, 
so it's high time to confess my sin.

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:14.630
As you intuited,

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:19.520
travelers, adventurers, and merchants would 
come by my inn, and I'd orchestrate their stays.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:20.760
<i>More like... <i>orc</i>hestrate.</i>

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:23.880
Tired from their long travels,

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:28.140
they'd go to their rooms, rest, 
and let down their guard...

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.280
Can it be...

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:30.520
That's right.

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:34.100
I'd take advantage of their vulnerable 
state and add <i>it</i> to their food!

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:34.890
Poison?!

00:08:34.890 --> 00:08:38.790
A secret orcish elixir of 
nutrition and stamina!

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:40.250
Nutrition... what?

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:41.490
That's not what I was expecting.

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:43.610
But it was a double-edged sword...

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:47.800
If I got the dose even slightly off, 
it put them in a state of total exhaustion!

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:53.440
I just wanted my customers to feel 
nice after a stay at my inn...

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:59.180
But one little mistake, 
and all my best intentions backfired!

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:01.040
Well, it's important to 
follow dosing instructions!

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.150
I'm a true swine who put 
his customers in danger!

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:05.430
What's wrong with me?

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:06.830
Hang on a minute.

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:08.150
Hey, Carla.

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:10.240
I think he might be a good guy after all!

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:13.660
You think we're the bad 
guys for upsetting him?

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:16.070
I see.

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:17.790
Then there's no two ways about it...

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:20.300
Guilty!

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:21.410
Just that one way, huh?

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:25.040
Oink! Please forgive me!

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:33.020
Alvin-san!

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:35.720
Are you going to sell me to slavers?

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:37.800
What have the slavers done to deserve that?

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:41.340
We're on a guild quest to 
collect medicinal herbs.

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:42.660
I see...

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:44.240
By the way, Alvin-san.

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:45.180
Yes?

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:48.680
Could you try to drag the 
cart a little smoother?

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:49.600
I'm motion-sick.

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:51.190
You don't have to ride in it!

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:53.990
What even made you think it was 
okay to get in the cart—

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:55.500
Alvin-san. Someone's here.

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:57.680
A traveler?

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:59.240
No, an old woman?

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.210
Do you think she's not feeling well?

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:03.290
Let's talk to her.

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:06.630
You're not going to make her 
pull the cart, are you?!

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:08.620
Why was <i>that</i> your assumption?!

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:10.250
Are you going to hit on her, then?

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:12.870
Don't make me say it again!

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:14.570
Excuse me.

00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:16.380
Are you all right?

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.770
Are you under the weather?

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:18.520
Hey, hey, hey!

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:20.180
Got time to kill, girl?

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:21.810
Wanna hang with us?

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:22.890
Don't hit on her!

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:26.620
It's so nice to see young 
folk with so much energy.

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:28.410
I'm just resting these old bones.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:30.680
But this place is infested with monsters!

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:32.660
We could take you home, if you like.

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:34.520
It wouldn't be too much trouble?

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:38.190
You use honeyed words to get 
close to women in trouble,

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:41.100
then cleverly steer the conversation 
into going home with them...

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:44.020
You're a true pick-up artist. 
And well-practiced, at that...

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:45.090
Phrasing, please!

00:10:45.090 --> 00:10:47.150
Yet you've never had a 
girlfriend! Mysterious!

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:48.440
Just butt out already!

00:10:48.740 --> 00:10:51.700
Well, at your kind insistence...

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:57.700
<i>Ho ho ho! The fool doesn't even 
realize I'm actually a witch!</i>

00:10:57.700 --> 00:11:02.290
<i>And I've been needing the 
bowels of a man for my brew!</i>

00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:03.580
You can walk.

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:05.930
That's a flag for a piggyback ride!

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:08.420
<i>And that one's a dark elf!</i>

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:11.280
<i>An extremely rare, high-quality ingredient!</i>

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:13.300
<i>I can't let her get away!</i>

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:15.570
Oh, young man...

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:17.090
I'll let you have this.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:18.590
What is it?

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:21.940
A homemade stamina potion.

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:23.700
I'd meant to drink it later,

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:25.420
but I'll give it to you instead.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:27.740
That's so kind of you!

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:29.680
<i>What a great fool!</i>

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:31.370
<i>That's a deadly poison!</i>

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:35.950
<i>And once I neutralize the man, 
the woman will be easily—</i>

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:36.710
What the...

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:38.130
What is it?

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:41.010
I'm having a hard time 
getting a grip on the cork.

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:44.130
Oh, come on. 
It's because of that ridiculous outfit!

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:46.580
Hand it to me. I'll open it.

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:47.620
Thanks.

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:48.750
No problem.

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:53.830
Goodness me. How did you ever get 
along without me, Alvin-san?

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:56.420
I don't know how I get along <i>with</i> you.

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:01.700
Bah!

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:04.020
What?!

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:07.070
What... What the hell did you do?!

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:09.390
G-Go on, Alvin-san!

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:10.780
Lap it up! Lap it up!

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:11.660
Like a dog!

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:12.580
Don't be ridiculous!

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:13.990
Three-second rule!

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:15.950
Pretty sure that doesn't apply to liquids!

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:19.700
Just because you can't open something 
is no reason to break it!

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:21.080
That's not what it was!

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:24.060
It was um... um...

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:25.850
Oh, yes! It's poison!

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:28.680
Poison? What?

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:30.700
Wait, you just told me to lap it up!

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:31.620
Fool!

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:33.100
Shut up, stupid!

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:35.600
You're simply too careless, Alvin-san!

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:37.790
Too trusting of strangers!

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:38.740
Well...

00:12:38.740 --> 00:12:40.430
Look at that sinister get-up!

00:12:40.430 --> 00:12:41.760
She's clearly a witch!

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:44.540
I mean, I won't pretend she 
doesn't look like one...

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:47.360
Though I'm not one to talk, 
bewitching as <i>I</i> am...

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:48.740
I'd argue that one!

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:51.810
Do you have any proof that I'm a witch?

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:53.130
Proof, you say?

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:54.930
Let me see!

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:56.470
I can get that by beating you up

00:12:56.470 --> 00:12:58.690
then making up whatever story I want!

00:12:58.690 --> 00:12:59.760
That's messed up!

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:04.550
But I suppose... it <i>is</i> a bit dangerous 
to trust a total stranger?

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:07.230
<i>Oh, no! My precious ingredients...</i>

00:13:07.230 --> 00:13:09.040
Oh, the sorrow!

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:13.760
I'd hoped to treat you to my fine home 
cooking when we arrived at my house.

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:16.270
My son died in an epidemic,

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:19.640
and I outlived my husband, 
so now I live all alone...

00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:25.350
To receive kindness after so long, I was 
simply so happy, I wanted to thank you!

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:28.750
Honestly. It's no use trying 
to earn our pity now.

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:31.450
We'd never believe such a ridiculous story.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:33.780
<i>Tch. I should've known it wouldn't work...</i>

00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:37.250
However, I do happen to 
be very hungry right now!

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:39.030
Now, hop aboard!

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:42.370
And after we get you home, you can 
pay us back with home cooking!

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:44.640
<i>Too easy.</i>

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:52.270
This here is my home.

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:55.020
Thanks for having us!

00:13:55.570 --> 00:13:57.050
So many books!

00:13:57.050 --> 00:14:00.180
I bet the place would burn real good!

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:02.020
Plotting your next crime, huh?

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:04.020
Have a seat wherever you like.

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:06.390
I'll prepare drinks for you all.

00:14:06.390 --> 00:14:07.530
Oh, thanks.

00:14:08.750 --> 00:14:11.030
Time to rest these old bones.

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:15.460
I'll have one from the tap!

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:16.410
What are you, an old man?

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:18.360
And <i>what</i> tap, exactly?

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:20.540
A tap on a fruit. For the juice.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:23.030
What an irritating bunch of children.

00:14:23.030 --> 00:14:24.300
But, no matter.

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:28.550
This anesthetic-infused herbal tea 
will make them nice and pliable!

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:32.920
Here you are. Herbal tea.

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:34.670
Is it made from "legal" herbs?

00:14:34.670 --> 00:14:36.570
Your own legality is questionable!

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:39.300
I'm sorry. 
She really likes to run her mouth.

00:14:39.300 --> 00:14:41.690
It's good to see young people 
with so much energy.

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:43.570
Here. Your herbal tea.

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:45.380
Oh, that's right.

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:46.690
Let's drink!

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:51.920
Are you okay?!

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:53.210
Oh, quite all right...

00:14:53.210 --> 00:14:55.080
Though it did get on my clothing...

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:58.080
And... are <i>you</i> okay?

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:02.670
Well... I was just thinking 
I'd like to lie down!

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:03.710
Could you not shout, maybe?

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:06.320
I was also thinking I'd 
like to read some books!

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:07.840
Would you clean them up already?

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:09.770
You go and get changed, ma'am.

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:12.040
I'll clean up here.

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:15.190
Thank you. You'll find the cleaning 
supplies right over there.

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:17.650
Tch. He's a lucky little rat.

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:20.120
Alvin-san, there's a rag right here.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:21.590
Oh, thanks.

00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:23.250
Hey, that's my mantle!

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:24.390
Quit messing around!

00:15:24.390 --> 00:15:27.030
I know. I'll try <i>that</i>!

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:29.780
All right, get cleaning already.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.400
Let's clean the room while we're at it.

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:34.160
It's really dusty and stuff.

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:37.590
I never thought I'd hear you 
offer to do something nice.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:42.190
Well, she lives by herself, so it's 
probably hard to keep the place clean...

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:44.220
<i>What's going on with her?</i>

00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:45.790
<i>She's being completely decent, for once!</i>

00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:50.140
And if I swiped a couple books in 
the meantime, who would notice?

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:52.430
Yeah, what else did I expect?

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:54.820
Now, what are we doing?

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:56.940
I figured we'd do some cleaning.

00:15:56.940 --> 00:15:58.630
Why, thank you!

00:15:58.630 --> 00:15:59.930
What is that, ma'am?

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:02.370
It's called an aromatic candle.

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:05.310
It puts out a fragrance that calms the soul!

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:07.260
I have visitors so rarely...

00:16:07.260 --> 00:16:10.260
I was hoping it might help you relax!

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:12.550
<i>In fact, it has a sedative effect!</i>

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:15.970
<i>I drank an antidote in 
advance, so I'll be fine.</i>

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:18.050
<i>But if they breathe it in 
for ten minutes straight,</i>

00:16:18.050 --> 00:16:21.280
<i>an unavoidable drowsiness 
will overtake them and—</i>

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:23.210
Fire safety first!

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:27.010
Oh...

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:31.480
Wh-What would you have done if 
the books had caught fire?!

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:34.550
At least warn someone before you do that!

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:36.140
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:38.980
I feel like I'm doing nothing 
but apologizing today!

00:16:38.980 --> 00:16:41.340
I'm sorry for being so 
dedicated to fire safety!

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:44.070
I'm sorry I failed to prevent 
this walking natural disaster!

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:46.540
I suppose I'll get changed again.

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:47.820
Oh? R-Right...

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:50.940
Thank goodness! She wasn't angry!

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:52.610
Like we'd get that lucky!

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:55.530
I think she's so far past 
anger she can't even yell!

00:16:55.890 --> 00:16:57.470
Let's clean up fast!

00:16:57.470 --> 00:17:00.820
When she gets back, we'll kneel before 
her, apologize, and be on our way!

00:17:00.820 --> 00:17:01.720
What?

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:05.270
I thought we were going to sit around the table, 
sharing fun stories and eating her cooking!

00:17:05.270 --> 00:17:08.280
You expect polite conversation 
in this frigid atmosphere?!

00:17:08.280 --> 00:17:10.980
What's all the hubbub here?

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:12.960
Ma'am, you're back already...

00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:16.840
I did promise to treat you to 
my home cooking, after all...

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:20.590
Actually, I was thinking 
we'd be on our way...

00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:22.490
Just eat already!

00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:24.340
<i>She's totally pissed!</i>

00:17:24.340 --> 00:17:25.830
<i>And what the heck is that?</i>

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:27.970
<i>She's totally here to kill us!</i>

00:17:27.970 --> 00:17:29.880
That looks gross.

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:31.470
Wish I hadn't gotten my hopes up.

00:17:31.470 --> 00:17:34.480
<i>And she keeps making everything worse!</i>

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:37.220
Would you like me to cast a 
spell to make it taste better?

00:17:37.220 --> 00:17:37.910
Eh?

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:39.260
Let's see...

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:41.130
I believe the chant goes like...

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:44.630
Become delicious! Moe, moe...

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:45.480
...Blast!

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:55.350
Just get out!

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:02.980
What in the world are you doing?

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:07.080
I just told you to leave!

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:08.740
What are you doing in here?

00:18:09.050 --> 00:18:11.340
Isn't it obvious?

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:13.170
I'm cooking something up.

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:15.120
<i>It sounds like you meant 
that in a different way!</i>

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:17.220
We had a set of bad breaks,

00:18:17.220 --> 00:18:20.110
and then I went and blew away your meal.

00:18:20.390 --> 00:18:22.730
And so, as atonement...

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:25.080
I will be cooking...

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:27.070
With components!

00:18:27.070 --> 00:18:28.070
Oh, shut up.

00:18:28.070 --> 00:18:29.940
Is there any way I can say no to this?

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:30.800
No!

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:33.120
Carla, have you ever cooked before?

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:34.080
No!

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:35.090
Yeah, I figured.

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:37.200
But I have <i>eaten</i> before!

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:38.210
Yeah, I figured!

00:18:39.190 --> 00:18:40.880
Do as you wish.

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:43.620
The ingredients are in 
the storehouse out back.

00:18:43.620 --> 00:18:45.210
Thank you very much!

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:48.150
Are you sure about this?

00:18:48.150 --> 00:18:52.470
Yes... It's clear she won't listen, 
no matter what I say.

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:56.370
But the sooner I let her do what she 
wants, the sooner she'll leave.

00:18:56.370 --> 00:18:58.330
Assuming we survive that long!

00:18:58.330 --> 00:18:59.820
Sorry for the wait!

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:02.140
It's amazing, Alvin-san!

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:04.990
She had so many ingredients 
I've never seen before!

00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:07.480
I've seen <i>that</i> one before!

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:09.590
Where have you been?!

00:19:09.590 --> 00:19:15.520
Well, after we left that beginner dungeon, 
I went chasing a butterfly, and got lost!

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:16.950
Hey, Carla!

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:19.620
You're not planning on 
cooking with <i>him</i>, are you?

00:19:19.620 --> 00:19:21.700
Oh, no. Not today.

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:23.410
Not <i>ever</i>, please!

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:24.820
So, what are you going to make?

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:26.740
I'll make myself a legend!

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:28.550
That's one legend no one will hand down!

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:30.430
Heave ho!

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:33.030
Hands to yourself, please.

00:19:31.610 --> 00:19:32.790
Heave ho!

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:35.700
Step right this way, ma'am!

00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:38.780
Just stand here and don't move.

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:41.990
What's this? I thought you were cooking...

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:43.260
Emergency Ratio—

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:45.530
Er, Altargaia-san, please help me.

00:19:45.860 --> 00:19:47.550
Roger-dodger!

00:19:47.550 --> 00:19:49.470
Put these ingredients over here,

00:19:49.470 --> 00:19:51.280
and those ingredients over there.

00:19:51.530 --> 00:19:53.660
There, that should do it.

00:19:53.990 --> 00:19:55.920
What exactly are you doing?

00:19:56.180 --> 00:19:59.580
Cooking requires the correct preparation 
of all ingredients, right?

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:02.660
I thought I'd supplement the 
preparation with a spell.

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:04.680
Is this going to be safe to eat?

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:06.230
No worries.

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:09.790
My cooking will be perfectly eatable. I think.

00:20:20.410 --> 00:20:21.400
Yes!

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:22.740
Don't say "Yes"!

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:23.550
What the hell is that?!

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:25.140
It just ate the old woman!

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:27.940
I said it would be <i>eatable</i>! 
You know, "able to eat"!

00:20:27.940 --> 00:20:30.650
That isn't how words work!

00:20:30.650 --> 00:20:33.470
And the only way that's cooking 
is if it's horri<i>frying</i>!

00:20:33.470 --> 00:20:36.490
Oh, that was good. 
"Well done," one might say.

00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:38.350
Seriously, we have to do something!

00:20:39.010 --> 00:20:40.410
Hey, did you just hear—

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:44.170
Looks like it's done.

00:20:44.460 --> 00:20:45.650
Are you all right, ma'am?!

00:20:45.650 --> 00:20:47.710
It didn't digest you, did it?

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:50.520
Where am I?

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:55.770
Who are you?

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:57.630
It's the old woman.

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:00.320
She sure doesn't look like an old woman!

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:04.480
I chose ingredients with 
anti-aging properties!

00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:07.780
I think that's a little much 
for food-based anti-aging!

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:09.000
Here.

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:11.670
Wh-Wh-What in the world has happened?!

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:15.200
How can I be young again? 
It's simply not possible!

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:18.420
A spell to restore youth... No, a ritual?

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:19.610
One way or another,

00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:24.420
the ability to reverse the flow of time is 
something I've only heard of in legends!

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:28.380
Who in the world are you?!

00:21:28.740 --> 00:21:30.170
Allow me to tell you.

00:21:30.170 --> 00:21:32.020
Carve these words into your heart!

00:21:32.810 --> 00:21:34.280
When standing, as stunning as—

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:34.280
Stress.

00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:36.640
When sitting, as striking as—

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:36.640
Depression.

00:21:37.410 --> 00:21:39.610
When walking, as arresting as—

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:39.610
Disaster!

00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:40.990
I am known as...

00:21:41.640 --> 00:21:42.510
...according to her...

00:21:42.510 --> 00:21:44.730
...the holy woman, Carla!

00:21:44.730 --> 00:21:45.420
Hey!

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:45.890
What now?!

00:21:45.890 --> 00:21:47.680
Stop riffing on everything I say!

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:48.610
They're in perfect sync.

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:48.990
Everything I said was true!

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:39.020
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:24.330 --> 00:23:26.490
I'll handle next episode's title!

00:23:26.490 --> 00:23:28.420
Hang on, you guys can read this stuff?!

00:23:29.630 --> 00:23:31.330
"As usual, Alvin and Carla 
have to overcome

00:23:31.330 --> 00:23:32.810
a series of crises on their travels

00:23:32.810 --> 00:23:34.020
like being attacked by a thief

00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:37.080
and running into a golem until
 a certain series of events..."

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:38.970
<b>See you then!</b>

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:39.090
<b>"As usual, Alvin and Carla have to overcome a series of crises on their
travels like being attacked by a thief and running into a golem until
 a certain series of events leads Alvin to take massive damage and
 it's so extreme that he even has to take off his armor to recuperate
 and that becomes an opportunity for them to get in a fight and
 reevaluate their relationship a little and even though their fights
 are an important part of the show the times being what they are
 during cast auditions and ADR and such only so many people
were allowed in the recording studio at once which is pretty 
tough to work around but everyone gave it their all to make 
the best show they could and that's the deal with episode 6."</b>

00:23:37.080 --> 00:23:38.290
Uh, that's the deal with episode 6!

00:23:38.290 --> 00:23:40.290
See you next—
